  <layout>One page of text in a single column; a marginal note in the left margin beside the paragraph beginning "Ut huc".</layout>
  <page_number>296</page_number>
  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>faci-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">ipso fortitudinem exserit,</l>
    <l n="2">quod temerarios suâ constan-</l>
    <l n="3">tiâ superet, quod propriis im-</l>
    <l n="4">peritet affectubus[?], neque ab iis</l>
    <l n="5">sese abripi patiatur.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Ut huc referri posset illud</l>
    <l n="7">Caji Marii, qui in bello civili</l>
    <l n="8">fossâ se cinxit, obsessumque</l>
    <l n="9">continuit, donec opportunam</l>
    <l n="10">erumpendi nactus esset occa-</l>
    <l n="11">sionem. Cumque Pompeus</l>
    <l n="12">Silo eum provocaret superba</l>
    <l n="13">voce, ac diceret: si magnus es</l>
    <l n="14">Imperator ô Mari, descende</l>
    <l n="15">in certamen: imo tu respon-</l>
    <l n="16">dit, si magnus es Imperator,</l>
    <l n="17">coge me vel invitum decerta-</l>
    <l n="18">re. Scilicet Marius Imperator</l>
    <l n="19">erat Maximus, quod alterius</l>
    <l n="20">provocationem contemtu</l>
    <l n="21">superasset. Et quis non duella</l>
    <l n="22">contemnet, qui consideret ea</l>
    <l n="23">non esse laude, sed vituperio</l>
    <l n="24">digna. Neque enim unquam</l>
    <l n="25">legimus historicos, in hono-</l>
    <l n="26">rem ejus, qui ad duella nimis</l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="left" at="Ut huc referri" line_from="6" line_to="6">Plutarch. in Apo-ptheg.</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>Uncertain readings: "affectubus" and "imperitet" (the line is slightly blurred at the word ends). The marginal note is printed as "Plutarch. in Apo-" / "ptheg." across two lines and is given as one note. The catchword "faci-" sits at the right below the last full line.</notes>
</page>
